<dialog id="privacy-policy-modal" class="hidden" open>
    <article>
        <header>
            <button id="close-privacy-modal" aria-label="Close"></button>
            <h2>Privacy Policy for AudioReaper</h2>
            <p>Last Updated: 02/07/2024</p>
        </header>
        <ol type="1">
            <li>
                <span><b>Introduction</b></span><br />
                Welcome to AudioReaper. This privacy policy explains our practices
                concerning the privacy of our visitors and users when using our software,
                which is designed as a personal project to showcase, grow, and improve
                skills in software development.
            </li>
            <li>
                <span><b>Information We Collect Temporarily</b></span><br />
                AudioReaper temporarily stores data such as access tokens and usernames
                in the backend session to facilitate the current user session. This
                data is strictly used to enhance user experience and is not used
                for any other purposes. All session data is wiped automatically at
                the end of the session and is not permanently stored anywhere.
            </li>
            <li>
                <span><b>Spotify API Interaction</b></span><br />
                AudioReaper uses the Spotify API to access and modify your Spotify
                playlists, but only in ways you have authorized. This may include
                reading your playlists and adding new songs to them. We do not access
                or alter any other aspects of your Spotify account. Your interaction
                with Spotify through our application is governed by the permissions
                you grant during the login process with Spotify.
            </li>
            <li>
                <span><b>Use of Your Information</b></span><br />
                Since no personal information is permanently collected or stored,
                there is no further use of such information beyond the current session.
            </li>
            <li>
                <span><b>Data Protection</b></span><br />
                We take precautions to ensure that any operations within the software
                and any temporary storage of data do not compromise the security
                of your device or any information therein.
            </li>
            <li>
                <span><b>Changes to Our Privacy Policy</b></span><br />
                We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. We encourage
                you to review this Privacy Policy periodically.
            </li>
            <li>
                <span><b>Contact Us</b></span><br />
                If you have any questions about this Privacy Policy, please contact
                us.
            </li>
        </ol>
    </article>
</dialog>
<script>
  import { attachModalLogic } from '../scripts/modalHandler';
  
  document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {
    attachModalLogic('.policy-trigger', 'privacy-policy-modal', '#close-privacy-modal');
  });
</script>